<title>UK: FORECAST - Reuters foreign exchange poll - Jan.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Reuters foreign exchange poll - Jan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The dollar is at its highest level for the year against the mark according to a Reuters poll of 35 banks and institutions from across the globe. The US currency is expected to fall against the mark during the next month to trade at 1.5646 before making some progress, climbing to 1.5706 marks</p>
<p>The following are the full results of Reuters' monthly foreign exchange poll.</p>
<p>The averages of the forecasts were as follows,</p>
<p>			   1-MTH	3-MTH	6-MTH	 12-MTH</p>
<p>    STERLING/DOLLAR  1.6852     1.6710     1.6636	1.6551</p>
<p>    DOLLAR/MARK	1.5646     1.5706     1.5583	1.5495</p>
<p>    DOLLAR/YEN	 115.41     114.01     112.71	110.70</p>
<p>Using the dollar forecasts above, the cross rates calculate at:--</p>
<p>			    1-MTH	3-MTH	6-MTH	12-MTH</p>
<p>    STERLING/MARK     2.6366     2.6245     2.5924     2.5645</p>
<p>    MARK/YEN	    73.76	72.61	72.33	 71.44</p>
<p>At 1106 GMT, the dollar was trading at 1.5705/15 marks and 115.75/76 yen. Sterling/dollar was quoted at $1.6900/10, sterling/mark at 2.6557/67 and mark/yen at 73.66/69.</p>
<p>The minimum and maximum forecasts were as follows --</p>
<p>    DOLLAR/MARK	1-MTH	3-MTH	6-MTH	 12-MTH</p>
<p>    MINIMUM	    1.5250     1.4800     1.4500	1.4000</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	    1.5900     1.8200     1.7000	1.7500</p>
<p>DOLLAR/YEN</p>
<p>    MINIMUM	    112.00     108.00     104.00	 95.00</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	    120.00     120.00     124.00	128.00</p>
<p>STERLING/DOLLAR</p>
<p>    MINIMUM	    1.6000     1.5823     1.5500	1.4400</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	    1.7125     1.7500     1.8000	1.8000</p>
<p>On average the forecasters expect dollar/yen to slip from current levels to trade at 115.41 in one month's time. It is then expected to progressively fall to trade at 110.70 in a year from now. The lowest level dollar/yen is expected to fall during that period is 95.00 yen.</p>
<p>The dollar is not expected to gain versus the mark, with forecasters expecting dollar/mark on average to stand at 1.5646 marks in one month and 1.5706 in three months.</p>
<p>It is then seen trading at around 1.5583 in six month's time before tailing off further to 1.5495 a year from now. The lowest dollar/mark is expected to fall during this period is 1.4000 marks.</p>
<p>The poll showed sterling will also make a steady decline. Forecasters expected cable to be trading at $1.6852 in one month's time and to weaken further to $1.6636 in six months, continuing its decline to $1.6551 this time next year.</p>
<p>The lowest level sterling is expected to fall is to $1.4400, in a year from now.</p>
<p>Rankings of the 35 forecasters by the accuracy of their one-month predictions will be published in the first week of February, just before the results of the next poll.</p>
